{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01D38EAfAGVgT1ows8ZCrLu6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified by differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The project stress-tests an AI code generation pipeline using Unix utilities as the subject.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` (one package per utility), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/sizeparse/` (size string parsing), `pkg/hashutil/` (checksums), `pkg/encutil/` (encoding). Specs live in `docs/specs/`.\n\n**Current state**: Many utilities are implemented across releases 00.0–09.1. Recent commits show cmd/stat (srd082) being actively implemented (R3.1, R4.1, R4.2, R5.1, R6.1, R7.1–R7.3). srd082 requirements are no longer in \"ready\" state.\n\n**Current release**: Release 10.0 is the earliest with \"ready\" requirements. Within 10.0:\n- stat (srd082): actively being implemented, no \"ready\" requirements remain\n- truncate (srd083): all 9 requirements ready, codestatus \"not started\"\n- link: no requirement states tracked — cannot propose\n- sync: already implemented\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nsrd083-truncate (release 10.0) is the only target with \"ready\" requirements in the earliest incomplete release. All 9 requirements (R1.1–R1.4, R2.1–R2.2, R3.1–R3.3) are ready. With the 4-sub-requirement-per-task constraint and mandatory implementation/test split, the minimum decomposition is 3 implementation tasks + 1 test task = 4 tasks (at the limit).\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight 1 for all srd083-truncate requirements (cannot read requirements.yaml per no-tool constraint):\n\n- Task 0: R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: R3.3(1) = 1 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: Test task (verifies all requirements)\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/truncate core file size operations (srd083 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml (SRD for truncate -- read requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - pkg/sizeparse/ (size string parsing with unit suffixes -- truncate uses SIZE with K/M/G suffixes)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler pattern -- all cmd/ utilities must call InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n      - cmd/stat/main.go (reference implementation of a similar file-metadata utility in this project)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/truncate/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: truncate command implementation -- core file truncation with --size flag and argument parsing\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd083 R1.1 -- parse command-line flags and positional arguments per the SRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd083 R1.2 -- set file size to the exact value specified by --size\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd083 R1.3 -- create files that do not exist when specified as arguments\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd083 R1.4 -- support --no-create (-c) to suppress file creation for nonexistent files\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use pkg/sizeparse.Parse or ParseWithOptions for --size argument parsing with unit suffixes\n      - id: D3\n        text: Use os.Truncate for setting file size after creating/opening the file\n      - id: D4\n        text: Exit codes and error messages must match GNU truncate behavior per the SRD\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/truncate/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/truncate/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/truncate/\" passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Running the binary with --size=100 on a new file creates a 100-byte file\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Running the binary with --no-create on a nonexistent file does not create it\n      - id: AC5\n        text: All four SRD requirements (R1.1 through R1.4) are implemented\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/truncate relative operations and reference (srd083 R2.1, R2.2, R3.1, R3.2)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml (SRD for truncate -- read requirements R2.1, R2.2, R3.1, R3.2)\n      - cmd/truncate/main.go (existing core implementation from prior task)\n      - pkg/sizeparse/ (size string parsing with unit suffixes)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/truncate/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add relative size operations (+/- prefixes), --reference flag, and error handling\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd083 R2.1 -- support relative size operations with +/- prefixes that grow or shrink the file relative to its current size\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd083 R2.2 -- support --reference (-r) to use another file's size as the base for size operations\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd083 R3.1 -- report errors for invalid size specifications and unreadable reference files with GNU-compatible messages\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd083 R3.2 -- process multiple file arguments, continuing on error per GNU behavior, with exit code reflecting whether any error occurred\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Relative sizes (+/-) are parsed from the --size value prefix before delegating unit parsing to sizeparse\n      - id: D2\n        text: When --reference is combined with --size, the size is relative to the reference file's size\n      - id: D3\n        text: Errors on individual files do not stop processing of remaining files -- exit code is nonzero if any file failed\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/truncate/\" compiles with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/truncate/\" passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Running with --size=+100 on a 50-byte file produces a 150-byte file\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Running with --reference=ref --size=+0 sets target to the reference file's size\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Running with an invalid --size value prints an error to stderr and exits nonzero\n      - id: AC6\n        text: Running with multiple files where one is invalid processes the valid files and exits nonzero\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/truncate version and help output (srd083 R3.3)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml (SRD for truncate -- read requirement R3.3)\n      - cmd/truncate/main.go (existing implementation from prior tasks)\n      - cmd/stat/main.go (reference for --help and --version output patterns)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/truncate/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Complete remaining requirement R3.3 per the SRD\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd083 R3.3 -- handle all remaining conditions specified in the SRD for this requirement\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Follow the exact error message format and exit code conventions from GNU truncate per the SRD\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/truncate/\" compiles with no errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/truncate/\" passes with no warnings\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All conditions specified in srd083 R3.3 are handled with correct behavior\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/truncate differential tests (srd083 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4, R2.1, R2.2, R3.1, R3.2, R3.3)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml (full SRD -- all requirements must have test coverage)\n      - cmd/truncate/main.go (implementation under test)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness -- DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function)\n      - cmd/stat/stat_test.go (reference test file for a similar file-metadata utility)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go truncate against gtruncate from Homebrew GNU coreutils\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Create TestDiff using testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") and exec.LookPath(\"gtruncate\") with t.Skip if reference binary not found\n      - id: R2\n        text: Write DiffTest cases covering all srd083 requirements R1.1 through R3.3 -- exact size, relative size (+/-), --reference, --no-create, multiple files, and error conditions\n      - id: R3\n        text: Verify exit code, stdout, and stderr match between Go and GNU binaries for each test case\n      - id: R4\n        text: Test edge cases including zero-byte truncation, nonexistent files with and without --no-create, and invalid --size values\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Use testutils.RunDiffTests for all differential test cases per project convention\n      - id: D2\n        text: Reference binary is gtruncate (Homebrew GNU coreutils with g-prefix)\n      - id: D3\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in test environment per project convention\n      - id: D4\n        text: Create temp files and directories in t.TempDir() for test fixtures -- do not leave test artifacts\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/truncate/ -count=1\" passes (or skips gracefully if gtruncate not found)\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Tests cover exact size, relative size (+/-), --reference, --no-create, multi-file processing, and error scenarios\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All test cases use the DiffTest/RunDiffTests pattern from pkg/testutils\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/truncate/\" passes with no warnings\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46672,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46672},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88c67b26-3ac3-434d-ab6e-ce7c4728dee4","uuid":"faba472d-4aca-4db4-8db8-e30875f1018f"}
